---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import { BRAND_NAME } from '~/lib/site';
import { getCities } from '~/lib/config';

const cities = getCities().filter((c) => c.launched);
---

<Base
  title={`About | ${BRAND_NAME}`}
  description="Deep, verified dog-friendly city guides — built one city at a time, starting with Tahoe City, CA."
>
  <div class="wrap prose page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Dog-friendly is the brand, not a filter</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      {BRAND_NAME} builds deep visitor guides for people who travel with their
      dogs. Not a checkbox on a hotel search — the whole guide, written from
      the dog's-eye view.
    </p>
    <p>
      Broad directories cover every city shallowly. We go the other way: one
      city at a time, covered deeply — the patios, trails, beaches, lodging,
      and local rules — with every dog policy verified against an official
      source and re-checked on a schedule.
    </p>
    <h2>Where we are today</h2>
    <ul>
      {cities.map((city) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`/${city.slug}/`}>{city.name}, {city.state_code}</a> — our launch city
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p>More cities are coming. Depth first, then breadth.</p>
    <h2>How we keep the lights on</h2>
    <p>
      The site is free to read. We earn money from display ads and from
      affiliate links on some bookings and activities — always disclosed,
      never affecting what we say about a venue's dog policy. Read the
      <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> and
      <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 2rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
